module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_primitive_actual_at_a_declared_container_is_unjudged

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CeilingNotStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_primitive_actual_at_a_declared_container_is_unjudged: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_primitive_actual_at_a_declared_container_is_unjudged" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingNotStated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an Accepted program in which a position declares a container application (List<T>, Map<K, V>) and the actual at that position is a PRIMITIVE. DESIGN section 4b names `values inhabit declared types` as part of the ordinary compiler floor, so an accepted pair here is below the floor, not a rung. The pair is not undecided and no diagnostic calls it unmodeled: none of the three positions measured emits a diagnostic naming this pair. (The compile does emit 193 unrelated advisories from dag/std/error_primitives.dag, one of which uses the phrase `declared-type inhabitance is UNMODELED at the direct call argument` for a different parameter; it is not about this pair.)",

    "SPECIMEN (remote runner linux/amd64, throwaway branch probe/row-resolve-twin at 3e7da683638f437402cd7ac16e43e3914c22159f = main 7d062bda1b6 plus the probe modules; `cargo build --release -p v1-compiler --bin gunbc`; 2026-11-07). Three positions, one pair each, all three ACCEPTED with `0 blocking error(s)` under `gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <file> --target dag --output-dir <dir>`: (1) let annotation -- `fn zz_let_ann() -> Bool { let items: List<String> = 5  true }`; (2) declared return -- `fn zz_ret() -> List<String> { 5 }`; (3) record-literal field, inside a `data ... : RecurringFailureMode` literal whose field is declared `List<DeclarationRef>` -- `evidence: 5,`, and its twin whose field is declared `List<String>` -- `receipts: 5,`. The same pair is also accepted under the evaluator: `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <row>.dag --function qn_probe` reaches the function lookup with no diagnostic.",

    "THE SAME PAIR AT THE FOURTH POSITION REFUSES, which is what makes this a missing arm rather than a general silence. `fn zz_take(xs: List<String>) -> Bool { true }` called as `zz_take(xs: 5)` is refused at BOTH instruments: `value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument for parameter 'xs': declared 'Container(List,Primitive(String))', produced 'Primitive(Int)'`. So the relation does own this pair's judgment at the call-argument position and lacks it at the other three, and the fix is the arm the call argument already has.",

    "NON-VACUITY CONTROLS, all four measured in the same build, because an accepted probe proves nothing unless a wrong one would be refused. (a) Function bodies in an entry module ARE elaborated: `fn zz_body_undef() -> Bool { zz_no_such_fn_zz() }` refuses `function 'zz_no_such_fn_zz' not found in scope`, and `fn zz_body_scalar() -> Bool { let flag: Bool = \"s\"  flag }` refuses `type mismatch: expected 'Coproduct(Bool)', got 'Primitive(String)'`. (b) The let-annotation position that accepted `let items: List<String> = 5` REFUSES `let flag: Bool = \"s\"` -- same position, same instrument, so the position is judged and only this pair slips. (c) Declared types that are not containers refuse a primitive actual at the record field: `identity: 5` where the field is declared `NonEmptyStr` refuses `type mismatch: expected 'Product(NonEmptyStr)', got 'Primitive(Int)'`, and `rung: 5` where it is declared `RungReading` refuses `expected 'Coproduct(RungReading)', got 'Primitive(Int)'`. (d) Container ELEMENTS refuse: `receipts: [5, \"...\"]` refuses `value does not inhabit its declared type at the list element: declared 'Primitive(String)', produced 'Primitive(Int)'` together with the field-level `declared 'Container(List,Primitive(String))', produced 'Container(List,Primitive(Int))'`, and `evidence: [5]` refuses the same way at `Product(DeclarationRef)`. So the four cells (non-container declared with non-container actual), (container declared with container actual), and (container element) are all judged; the single unjudged cell is container-declared against non-container actual.",

    "WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED, stated so a later reader does not over-read this row. Only `Int` literals were measured as the actual, against `List<String>` and `List<DeclarationRef>`; `Map<K, V>` and other containers are inferred from the shared `Container(List, T)` shape in the diagnostics, not measured. The record-field specimens are `data` literal fields; a `type` record literal at the same pair was not measured, and `record_field_admits_a_distinct_product_value` measures a different actual shape at a nominal field. The rung is UNREAD: acceptance is established, no ceiling is, so no StructurallyGuaranteed standing is claimed here even though the sibling row `a_declared_container_type_is_checked_by_head_only` states one for the pair it owns. And the evaluator's exit code at the three function positions is NOT a type verdict: `gunbc run` returns rc=2 there with `returned 'true', not 'ProcessExit'`, which is the host refusing to map a non-verdict to an exit code (the same stop-visibly rule that makes a Bool claim refuse), so `gunbc compile` is the authority for a position inside a function body.",

    "RELATION TO THE ROWS THAT ALREADY OWN PART OF THIS CHAIN, so the class is not double-counted. `a_declared_container_type_is_checked_by_head_only` owns the case where BOTH sides are containers whose type arguments disagree (`let q: Map<Bool, Bool> = m` with `m: Map<String, Int>`); its CLIMB records that gunbc#15595 routed the record-literal field through declared_type_obligation_diags and took that witness from 12 of 13 to 13 of 13, and it names its residual as positions with no obligation producer. This row is the cell its 13 of 13 does not reach: the actual is not a container at all. `record_field_admits_a_distinct_product_value` owns a non-literal value of a distinct nominal product at a nominal field, and records that a record LITERAL there does refuse, its diagnosis being that the field position consults a local chain that never asks the nominal-product relation the call argument shares. This row is neither of those actuals and neither of those declared shapes. The compiler's own advisory vocabulary already names the general shape -- `declared-type inhabitance is UNMODELED ... no arm of the relation judges this pair yet` appears as an advisory elsewhere in the same compile -- so an absent arm is a recognised condition; what is missing is an arm for this pair at these three positions.",

    "REVIEW TELL: a declared-type relation that refuses a pair at one position and is silent at its siblings, discovered by asking not `does this position check types` but `does EVERY position consult the SAME relation` -- and by refusing to accept a green probe until a probe that must be red has been shown to be red.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
